.TH SCD-VAULT-CHECK 1 "2026-08-13" "SCD Reporting v0.2.0" "SCD Reporting"
.SH NAME
scd-vault-check \- verify the Vault secret layout that SCD Reporting loads at startup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./scripts/scd-vault-check
[\fB\-e\fR \fIENV\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-a\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-show\-missing\fR]
[\fB\-q\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scd-vault-check
answers the question "will the pod actually get its secrets?" without starting
Django, building an image, or deploying anything. It authenticates to Vault
exactly as the application does, walks the same section map defined in
.IR scd_reporting/vault.py ,
and reports for every mapped key whether it resolves, which environment
variable it would populate, and whether an existing environment variable would
shadow it.
.PP
Secret values are never printed. Each resolved key is reported with its length
and the first eight hex characters of its SHA\-256 digest, which is enough to
confirm that two environments hold different values, or that a rotation
actually took effect, without exposing the secret itself.
.SH SECRET LAYOUT
Secrets are stored one KV v2 secret per service beneath a per\-environment
prefix:
.PP
.RS
.nf
okd/shared/<env>/scd\-reporting/anthropic   api_key
okd/shared/<env>/scd\-reporting/django      secret_key, initial_admin_password
okd/shared/<env>/scd\-reporting/email       password
okd/shared/<env>/scd\-reporting/google      client_secret
okd/shared/<env>/scd\-reporting/oidc        client_secret
okd/shared/<env>/scd\-reporting/postgres    password
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sections that do not exist are skipped silently; only sections that exist but
cannot be read are reported as problems. This is deliberate \(em the
.I github
section is part of the shared house layout but is not populated for this
application.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-env " " \fIENV\fR
Shorthand for the standard path of a known environment.
.I ENV
is
.B test
or
.BR prod ,
expanding to
.I okd/shared/test/scd\-reporting
and
.I okd/shared/prod/scd\-reporting
respectively.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-path " " \fIPATH\fR
Explicit KV v2 prefix, mount included, for a path not covered by
.BR \-\-env .
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-addr " " \fIADDR\fR
Vault server address. Defaults to
.BR $VAULT_ADDR .
.TP
.B \-\-show\-missing
Also list sections and keys that are absent. Useful when a secret appears not
to reach the application and you need to tell "key missing" from "key shadowed".
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress all output and communicate only through the exit status, for use in
scripts.
.SH CONFIGURATION PRECEDENCE
Command line, then environment, then built\-in default:
.BR \-\-addr " > " $VAULT_ADDR ,
and
.BR \-\-path " > " \-\-env " > " $VAULT_SECRET_PATH .
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Credentials are resolved the same way the application resolves them:
.B $VAULT_TOKEN
if set, otherwise an AppRole login using
.B $VAULT_ROLE_ID
and
.BR $VAULT_SECRET_ID ,
with the auth mount taken from
.B $VAULT_APPROLE_MOUNT
(default
.IR auth/approle ).
For interactive use, your personal Vault session is normally sufficient:
.PP
.RS
.nf
export VAULT_ADDR=https://ssivault.fnal.gov:8200
export VAULT_TOKEN=$(vault print token)
\&./scripts/scd\-vault\-check \-\-env prod
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every section that exists was readable.
.TP
.B 1
At least one section exists but could not be read, typically a policy problem.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error \(em no address or no secret path was supplied.
.TP
.B 3
Could not connect to or authenticate against Vault.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check production before a deploy:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&./scripts/scd\-vault\-check \-\-env prod
.fi
.RE
.PP
Confirm test and prod hold genuinely different values \(em compare the
fingerprint columns:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&./scripts/scd\-vault\-check \-\-env test
\&./scripts/scd\-vault\-check \-\-env prod
.fi
.RE
.PP
Diagnose a secret that is not reaching the application, including the ones
being shadowed by the local environment:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&./scripts/scd\-vault\-check \-\-env prod \-\-show\-missing
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I scd_reporting/vault.py
Defines
.BR SECRET_MAP ,
the single source of truth for the section\-to\-environment\-variable mapping
that this tool and the application both use.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR get-vault-apptoken (1),
.BR deploy (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman
